    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:amidah/avot">
        <tei:pb ed="1965" n="6" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n14_medium.jpg"/>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:amidah/avot/barukh_attah"/>Blessed art Thou, O Lord our God and the God of our fathers, the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac and the God of Jacob, the great, mighty and awe-inspiring God, God the Most High, who performs acts of kindness and owns everything and remembers the good deeds of the fathers and will bring a redeemer for their children’s children for His Name’s sake in love.</tei:p>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:amidah/avot/zokhrenu"/>Remember us for life, O King who delights in life, and inscribe us in the book of life for Thy sake, O living God. <tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:amidah/avot/magen_avraham"/>O King, helper and saviour and shield, blessed art Thou, O Lord, the shield of Abraham.<tei:milestone unit="prayer-part"/></tei:p>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
